        {
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain",
          "findings": [
            {
              "message": "Gate 10 now permits user-approved Accepted Deviations, but this workflow and the Claude adapter still state that Phase 0 is the only user-confirmation pause. The delegated `pr-review` workflow explicitly waits for user approval before accepting deviations, so the new terminal branch contradicts adr2pr's autonomy contract. Either retain machine PASS as the only adr2pr terminal state or consistently declare Accepted Deviations as another approval exception.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": ".harness/workflows/track/adr2pr.md",
              "line": 194,
              "category": "command wiring breakage"
            },
            {
              "message": "The broadened terminal contract was not propagated to the Codex adapter: `.agents/skills/track-adr2pr/SKILL.md:52` still permits successful completion only for a zero-findings terminal state. A user-approved Accepted Deviations result is therefore terminal in the workflow SSoT but not in its adapter. Remove the duplicated gate condition from the adapter or align it with the SSoT.",
              "severity": "P1",
              "file": ".harness/workflows/track/adr2pr.md",
              "line": 194,
              "category": "adapter-SSoT synchronization"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:2cc0458a263097904553831e122a12a48b422da376d5fc6cad0247560435d5ed",
          "at": "2026-07-18T06:38:52Z"
